// Orbit — circular motion around a point or another object.
// A tiny solar system: the planet circles the sun, and the moon circles
// the planet inside a group that rides along.

theme clay

sphere sun r(0.8) at(0 2 0) color(gold)

group system at(3 2 0)
sphere planet r(0.35) in(system) at(0 0 0) color(steelblue)
sphere moon   r(0.12) in(system) at(0.9 0 0) color(#cfcfcf)

orbit system around(sun) by(360) over(12)    // one lap of the sun
orbit moon around(planet) by(1080) over(12)  // three laps of the planet

// The comet loops vertically — axis(x) tips the circle on its side.
sphere comet r(0.1) at(0 2 1.8) color(orchid)
orbit comet around(sun) axis(x) by(720) over(12)

// An eclipse is a sight-line fact: at t=0 the planet and moon sit
// exactly between the watcher and the sun. Scrub time and watch it clear.
sphere watcher r(0.2) at(6 2 0) color(tomato)

? sees(watcher sun)
? blocked-by(watcher sun)
? distance(moon sun)
